  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Responsiveness in Detail**\n\nI\'ve been examining the responsiveness across a slider range from 1.00 to 2.40. Notably, at p=1.00, it\'s remarkably responsive while maintaining C1-smoothness at the center and boundaries. I\'m noting the mapping from the slider to resulting value: 0.25 -> 0.0918, 0.50 -> 0.4150, 0.75 -> 0.8038, 0.90 -> 0.9639, 1.00 -> 1.0000.\n\n\n**Refining Parameter Interactions**\n\nI\'m now examining how the parameter p, specifically at 1.35, 1.80, and 2.40, affects responsiveness. I\'m noting significant changes to the output values. At p=1.35, I see the values 0.25 -> 0.0316, 0.50 -> 0.2628, 0.75 -> 0.7006, 0.90 -> 0.9384, 1.00 -> 1.0000.  Then, at p=1.80: 0.25 -> 0.0078, 0.50 -> 0.1416, 0.75 -> 0.5733, 0.90 -> 0.8994, 1.00 -> 1.0000.  Finally, at p=2.40: 0.25 -> 0.0012, 0.50 -> 0.0602, 0.75 -> 0.4269, 0.90 -> 0.8404, 1.00 -> 1.0000. I also need to verify that existing code doesn\'t unintentionally add discontinuities.\n\n\n**Confirming Boundary Conditions**\n\nI\'m now certain about global C1-continuity. Specifically, the reticle\'s transition behaviors seem well-defined. The `AimBoundary.ts` code is consistent with the goal of creating a smooth visual output, and the code confirms smooth operation across all boundaries. Furthermore, changes to the reticle size do not affect the Steering variables, and code is designed to not modify the Flight HUD.\n\n\n**Verifying Implementation Integration**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `SteeringCurvePreview` directly utilizes the refined C1 S-curve via `evaluateResponseCurveScalar`, ensuring the live preview in the Settings Panel accurately reflects the adjustments. I\'m also going through the strict preservation requirements to guarantee the implementation doesn\'t affect critical existing components such as pointer lock, input handling, edge continuity, reticle behavior, aim boundary, and other unrelated elements. I\'m focusing on ensuring these modules remain untouched.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "vDz_aqeXIP29qtsPvNC_mA8"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_18041808013793476303"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Refine evaluateResponseCurveScalar in AimBoundary.ts to a globally C1-continuous monotonic S-curve (smoothstep over u^p with inner precision shaping) for fine center aiming and zero derivative jump at the aim boundary.\", \"EndLine\":326, \"Instruction\":\"Update evaluateResponseCurveScalar to shape smoothstep(u^p) with precisionSensitivity so both deadzone exit (r=dz) and boundary saturation (r=1) are C1-continuous with zero slope spike.\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"/**\\n * Pure scalar radial response curve for normalized virtual joystick magnitude r >= 0.\\n *\\n * - r <= deadzone: returns 0 (clean drift-free center).\\n * - deadzone < r < 1: strictly monotonic, globally C1-continuous S-curve that keeps\\n *   center sensitivity very low for precise aiming, ramps smoothly through mid-deflection,\\n *   and eases its slope cleanly to zero as r -> 1 so reaching the aim boundary never\\n *   produces an abrupt turn-rate surge.\\n * - r >= 1: saturates cleanly at maxSteeringInput (zero runaway sensitivity beyond radius).\\n */\\nexport function evaluateResponseCurveScalar(\\n  radialMagnitude: number,\\n  deadzone: number = STEERING_CONFIG.deadzone,\\n  responseCurve: number = STEERING_CONFIG.responseCurve,\\n  precisionSensitivity: number = STEERING_CONFIG.precisionSensitivity,\\n  maxSteeringInput: number = STEERING_CONFIG.maxSteeringInput,\\n): number {\\n  const dz = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(\\n    deadzone,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.deadzone.min,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.deadzone.max,\\n  );\\n  const maxOut = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(\\n    maxSteeringInput,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.maxSteeringInput.min,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.maxSteeringInput.max,\\n  );\\n\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(radialMagnitude) || radialMagnitude <= dz) {\\n    return 0;\\n  }\\n  if (radialMagnitude >= 1) {\\n    return maxOut;\\n  }\\n\\n  const p = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(\\n    responseCurve,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.responseCurve.min,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.responseCurve.max,\\n  );\\n  const k = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(\\n    precisionSensitivity,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.precisionSensitivity.min,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.precisionSensitivity.max,\\n  );\\n\\n  const u = (radialMagnitude - dz) / Math.max(1e-5, 1 - dz);\\n  const t = Math.pow(u, p);\\n  const smooth = t * t * (3 - 2 * t);\\n  const shaped = smooth * (k + (1 - k) * smooth);\\n  return THREE.MathUtils.clamp(shaped, 0, 1) * maxOut;\\n}\", \"StartLine\":277, \"TargetContent\":\"/**\\n * Pure scalar radial response curve for normalized virtual joystick magnitude r >= 0.\\n *\\n * - r <= deadzone: returns 0 (clean drift-free center).\\n * - deadzone < r < 1: strictly monotonic, C1-smooth conservative curve combining\\n *   responseCurve exponent and gentle inner precisionSensitivity shaping.\\n * - r >= 1: saturates cleanly at maxSteeringInput (zero runaway sensitivity beyond radius).\\n */\\nexport function evaluateResponseCurveScalar(\\n  radialMagnitude: number,\\n  deadzone: number = STEERING_CONFIG.deadzone,\\n  responseCurve: number = STEERING_CONFIG.responseCurve,\\n  precisionSensitivity: number = STEERING_CONFIG.precisionSensitivity,\\n  maxSteeringInput: number = STEERING_CONFIG.maxSteeringInput,\\n): number {\\n  const dz = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(\\n    deadzone,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.deadzone.min,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.deadzone.max,\\n  );\\n  const maxOut = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(\\n    maxSteeringInput,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.maxSteeringInput.min,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.maxSteeringInput.max,\\n  );\\n\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(radialMagnitude) || radialMagnitude <= dz) {\\n    return 0;\\n  }\\n  if (radialMagnitude >= 1) {\\n    return maxOut;\\n  }\\n\\n  const p = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(\\n    responseCurve,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.responseCurve.min,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.responseCurve.max,\\n  );\\n  const k = THREE.MathUtils.clamp(\\n    precisionSensitivity,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.precisionSensitivity.min,\\n    STEERING_BOUNDS.precisionSensitivity.max,\\n  );\\n\\n  const u = (radialMagnitude - dz) / Math.max(1e-5, 1 - dz);\\n  const smooth = u * u * (3 - 2 * u);\\n  const shaped = Math.pow(u, p) * (k + (1 - k) * smooth);\\n  return THREE.MathUtils.clamp(shaped, 0, 1) * maxOut;\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/engine/AimBoundary.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating steering response curve\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update steering response curve\"}"
