  planner_response {
    response: "### Step 1 \342\200\224 Pipeline Inspection & Root Cause\n\nTracing the steering pipeline across `InputManager.ts`, `FlightController.ts`, `AimBoundary.ts`, and `steering.ts`:\n\n1. **Pointer Lock & Mouse Deltas** (`src/engine/InputManager.ts`): Accumulates relative `event.movementX` / `event.movementY` only while Pointer Lock is owned by the canvas, without absolute cursor coupling or recentering.\n2. **Reticle Displacement & Aim Boundary Clamp** (`src/engine/FlightController.ts`, `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`): Adds scaled relative deltas (`inputScale = mouseSensitivity * clamp(vh / 720, 0.5, 2.5)`) to `(joystickX, joystickY)` and projects the result onto the centered `30% \303\227 35%` rounded-rectangle boundary via `clampToRoundedRect`.\n3. **Boundary Normalization** (`evaluateVirtualJoystick` in `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`): Computes exact radial fraction `r = clamp(dist / computeRoundedRectRayRadius(ux, uy, boundary), 0, 1)`.\n4. **Steering Response Mapping** (`evaluateResponseCurveScalar` in `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`): Maps `r` to normalized steering magnitude in `[0, maxSteeringInput]`.\n5. **Angular Integration** (`FlightController.ts`): Scales `(steerX, steerY)` by `yawSensitivity` / `pitchSensitivity` and `profile.yawSpeed` / `profile.pitchSpeed`, then tracks target rates via `stepAngularVelocity`.\n\n**Root Cause of Both Reported Issues** (localized solely to `evaluateResponseCurveScalar` in `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`; `clampToRoundedRect`, `computeRoundedRectRayRadius`, `steeringZone`, `InputManager`, and `stepAngularVelocity` had no sudden multiplier switch or competing calculation):\n\n- **Excessive center rotation**: With `deadzone = 0.06`, `responseCurve (p) = 1.35`, and `precisionSensitivity (k) = 0.85`, the previous formula `u^p * (k + (1 - k) * smoothstep(u))` rose rapidly immediately outside the 6% deadzone (`slope = 0.405` at `r = 0.10` and `0.728` at `r = 0.25`, already producing `10.0%` of full turn rate at 25% deflection).\n- **Abrupt boundary behavior**: The previous curve accelerated monotonically up to its steepest slope (`~1.45`) right into `r = 1.0`, hitting a sharp C\302\271 derivative corner (`1.436 -> 0`) at the boundary clamp rather than easing smoothly into saturation.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2 & 4 \342\200\224 Source Change & Calibration Comparison\n\n**File Modified:** `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts` (`evaluateResponseCurveScalar`, lines 277\342\200\223327)\n\nReplaced the inner-steep / boundary-corner mapping with a globally C\302\271-continuous, strictly monotonic S-curve using the existing `responseCurve` (`1.35`), `precisionSensitivity` (`0.85`), `deadzone` (`0.06`), and `maxSteeringInput` (`1.0`) parameters:\n\n```ts\nconst u = (radialMagnitude - dz) / Math.max(1e-5, 1 - dz);\nconst t = Math.pow(u, p);\nconst smooth = t * t * (3 - 2 * t);\nconst shaped = smooth * (k + (1 - k) * smooth);\n```\n\n- At `r = dz`: `f(dz) = 0` and `f\'(dz\342\201\272) = 0`.\n- At `r = 1.0`: `f(1) = maxOut` and `f\'(1\342\201\273) = 0`, matching the flat `r > 1` region (`f\'(1\342\201\272) = 0`) with zero turn-rate surge or slope corner at the boundary.\n- All maximum turn rates (`yawSpeed`, `pitchSpeed`), overall sensitivity (`mouseSensitivity`, `yawRate`, `pitchRate`), Pointer Lock handling, `movementX`/`movementY` handling, boundary geometry, HUD, camera, combat, bots, and missions were left untouched.\n\n#### Calibration Table (`dz = 0.06`, `p = 1.35`, `k = 0.85`, `maxOut = 1.0`)\n\n| Boundary Position (`r`) | Previous Output (Slope) | Refined Output (Slope) | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Center (`0.00`) | `0.0000` (`0.00`) | `0.0000` (`0.00`) | Drift-free center |\n| Deadzone Edge (`0.06`) | `0.0000` (`0.04`) | `0.0000` (`0.00`) | Zero breakaway jump |\n| `15%` (`0.15`) | `0.0360` (`0.54`) | `0.0044` (`0.13`) | ~8x finer micro-aiming near center |\n| `25%` (`0.25`) | `0.1000` (`0.73`) | `0.0316` (`0.43`) | ~3.2x calmer small-movement tracking |\n| `50%` (`0.50`) | `0.3294` (`1.10`) | `0.2628` (`1.43`) | Smooth, progressive mid-range turn ramp |\n| `75%` (`0.75`) | `0.6415` (`1.38`) | `0.7006` (`1.86`) | Strong outer tracking authority |\n| `95%` (`0.95`) | `0.9277` (`1.45`) | `0.9834` (`0.64`) | Smooth deceleration of slope before edge |\n| `100%` (`1.00`) | `1.0000` (`1.44 -> 0` corner) | `1.0000` (`0.00`) | Full turn rate, C\302\271-smooth boundary entry |\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Browser Test Status\n\n- **Build (`compile_applet` / `vite build`)**: Passed.\n- **Type Check (`lint_applet` / `tsc --noEmit`)**: Passed with 0 errors.\n- **Curve & Boundary Continuity Check (`npx tsx`)**: Verified monotonic output across 10,000 samples in `[0, 1.25]` (max step `0.000237` per `dr = 0.000125`) and continuous `evaluateVirtualJoystick` / `clampToRoundedRect` output across `[0\302\260, 22.5\302\260, 45\302\260, 67.5\302\260, 90\302\260]`.\n- **Real Browser Gameplay Validation**: **Unverified** \342\200\224 no browser runtime (`chromium`, `google-chrome`, `playwright`) or physical mouse input device is available in this environment. Acceptance tests 1\342\200\2237 require live verification in a desktop browser with Pointer Lock and a real mouse."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Browser Limitations**\n\nI\'ve been examining the verification output and the absence of browser paths from `which`. It\'s now evident that true browser interaction, involving a physical mouse, is not available in this headless CLI environment. This forces a shift toward a more explicit and honest approach to testing.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "7Tz_apTvD9Khz7IPmcK4sQs"
    modified_response: "### Step 1 \342\200\224 Pipeline Inspection & Root Cause\n\nTracing the steering pipeline across `InputManager.ts`, `FlightController.ts`, `AimBoundary.ts`, and `steering.ts`:\n\n1. **Pointer Lock & Mouse Deltas** (`src/engine/InputManager.ts`): Accumulates relative `event.movementX` / `event.movementY` only while Pointer Lock is owned by the canvas, without absolute cursor coupling or recentering.\n2. **Reticle Displacement & Aim Boundary Clamp** (`src/engine/FlightController.ts`, `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`): Adds scaled relative deltas (`inputScale = mouseSensitivity * clamp(vh / 720, 0.5, 2.5)`) to `(joystickX, joystickY)` and projects the result onto the centered `30% \303\227 35%` rounded-rectangle boundary via `clampToRoundedRect`.\n3. **Boundary Normalization** (`evaluateVirtualJoystick` in `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`): Computes exact radial fraction `r = clamp(dist / computeRoundedRectRayRadius(ux, uy, boundary), 0, 1)`.\n4. **Steering Response Mapping** (`evaluateResponseCurveScalar` in `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`): Maps `r` to normalized steering magnitude in `[0, maxSteeringInput]`.\n5. **Angular Integration** (`FlightController.ts`): Scales `(steerX, steerY)` by `yawSensitivity` / `pitchSensitivity` and `profile.yawSpeed` / `profile.pitchSpeed`, then tracks target rates via `stepAngularVelocity`.\n\n**Root Cause of Both Reported Issues** (localized solely to `evaluateResponseCurveScalar` in `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`; `clampToRoundedRect`, `computeRoundedRectRayRadius`, `steeringZone`, `InputManager`, and `stepAngularVelocity` had no sudden multiplier switch or competing calculation):\n\n- **Excessive center rotation**: With `deadzone = 0.06`, `responseCurve (p) = 1.35`, and `precisionSensitivity (k) = 0.85`, the previous formula `u^p * (k + (1 - k) * smoothstep(u))` rose rapidly immediately outside the 6% deadzone (`slope = 0.405` at `r = 0.10` and `0.728` at `r = 0.25`, already producing `10.0%` of full turn rate at 25% deflection).\n- **Abrupt boundary behavior**: The previous curve accelerated monotonically up to its steepest slope (`~1.45`) right into `r = 1.0`, hitting a sharp C\302\271 derivative corner (`1.436 -> 0`) at the boundary clamp rather than easing smoothly into saturation.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2 & 4 \342\200\224 Source Change & Calibration Comparison\n\n**File Modified:** `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts` (`evaluateResponseCurveScalar`, lines 277\342\200\223327)\n\nReplaced the inner-steep / boundary-corner mapping with a globally C\302\271-continuous, strictly monotonic S-curve using the existing `responseCurve` (`1.35`), `precisionSensitivity` (`0.85`), `deadzone` (`0.06`), and `maxSteeringInput` (`1.0`) parameters:\n\n```ts\nconst u = (radialMagnitude - dz) / Math.max(1e-5, 1 - dz);\nconst t = Math.pow(u, p);\nconst smooth = t * t * (3 - 2 * t);\nconst shaped = smooth * (k + (1 - k) * smooth);\n```\n\n- At `r = dz`: `f(dz) = 0` and `f\'(dz\342\201\272) = 0`.\n- At `r = 1.0`: `f(1) = maxOut` and `f\'(1\342\201\273) = 0`, matching the flat `r > 1` region (`f\'(1\342\201\272) = 0`) with zero turn-rate surge or slope corner at the boundary.\n- All maximum turn rates (`yawSpeed`, `pitchSpeed`), overall sensitivity (`mouseSensitivity`, `yawRate`, `pitchRate`), Pointer Lock handling, `movementX`/`movementY` handling, boundary geometry, HUD, camera, combat, bots, and missions were left untouched.\n\n#### Calibration Table (`dz = 0.06`, `p = 1.35`, `k = 0.85`, `maxOut = 1.0`)\n\n| Boundary Position (`r`) | Previous Output (Slope) | Refined Output (Slope) | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Center (`0.00`) | `0.0000` (`0.00`) | `0.0000` (`0.00`) | Drift-free center |\n| Deadzone Edge (`0.06`) | `0.0000` (`0.04`) | `0.0000` (`0.00`) | Zero breakaway jump |\n| `15%` (`0.15`) | `0.0360` (`0.54`) | `0.0044` (`0.13`) | ~8x finer micro-aiming near center |\n| `25%` (`0.25`) | `0.1000` (`0.73`) | `0.0316` (`0.43`) | ~3.2x calmer small-movement tracking |\n| `50%` (`0.50`) | `0.3294` (`1.1